<file path="webui/docs/UI rules.txt">
ROLE: Expert Svelte Frontend Developer & UI/UX Designer. PROJECT: Echosync (Music Sync & Manager). STACK: Svelte (Latest), CSS Variables for Theming.
CORE DESIGN PHILOSOPHY: Modern, clean, data-dense but breathable. Avoid "noisy" UI. Prioritize visual hierarchy—users should see what they are editing clearly.

1. COLOR PALETTE (DARK MODE DEFAULT) Use CSS variables for all colors to support future theming.
Primary Accent: Neon Mint (#00E676 or similar based on your screenshot). Used for: Active states, primary buttons, toggles, progress bars.
Background - App: Deep Void (#0a0a0c - almost black, not gray).
Background - Surface/Cards: Dark Blue-Grey (#13151a). Used for: Settings panels, sidebars, modal backgrounds.
Background - Input: Darker Recess (#08080a). Used for: Text fields, dropdowns.
Text - Primary: White (#ffffff). High contrast for headers/labels.
Text - Secondary: Muted Grey (#8b9bb4). For descriptions, placeholders, and unselected icons.
Status - Error: Soft Red (#ff5252).
Status - Success: Matches Primary Accent.
2. COMPONENT RULES
Cards: Use the "Surface" color. rounded-xl (approx 12px-16px). Subtle border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05).
Buttons
Primary: Solid Neon Mint, Black Text (for contrast). Bold font. Rounded-md.
Secondary/Ghost: Transparent background, White text, Thin border or hover effect only.
Inputs: High height (48px) for touch targets. Background "Darker Recess". Border 1px solid #333. Focus state must glow with Primary Accent.
Typography: Sans-serif (Inter/Roboto).
Headers: Bold, tight spacing.
Labels: Uppercase, small, tracking-wide (letter-spacing), muted color.

3. LAYOUT & RESPONSIVENESS
Mobile-First: All flex/grid layouts must stack vertically on screens < 768px.
Touch Targets: All clickable elements (buttons, inputs, icons) must be at least 44x44px.
Spacing: Use generous padding inside cards (p-6) to separate content.
The Sidebar Problem Your new sidebar looks great on desktop, but it will take up 50% of a phone screen.
Suggestion: On mobile (< 768px), convert the Sidebar into a Bottom Navigation Bar for high-level items (Dashboard, Sync, Search, Settings).

3. "Secret" Inputs (API Keys)
Suggestion: For fields like Client Secret or User Token, use an "Eye" toggle to mask the text by default (display ••••••••).

4. Feedback is Key
Suggestion: When a user hits "Save All" in your new UI, don't just reload. Show a Toast Notification (a small popup at the bottom/top right) that says "Settings Saved Successfully" in your Mint Green color.

5. The "Browse" Buttons In your screenshot, you have "Browse" buttons for directories (/app/downloads).
Mobile Issue: Browsing a server filesystem on a phone touchscreen is hard if the click targets are small.
Suggestion: Make the file picker a Modal that covers the screen, with large folders you can tap easily, rather than a tiny dropdown list.

